  "rulesRegulationsTitle": "Rules & Regulations",
  "rule1": "1. Pratap Gaurav Kendra Rashtriya Tirth will open Everyday for Audience.",
  "rule2": "2. Ticket window will be opened for audience at 9.30 am to 6.pm.",
  "rule3": "3. Duration of all exhibition and robotic show visit in Pratap Gaurav Kendra approx one and half hours.",
  "rule4": "4. To maintain Pratap Gaurav Kendra Ticket Per Person above 12 years is 160/- only for General Show and with family 0-5 year child is free and 110/- Ticket for 6-12 year child. Major Attraction Live Water Laser Show, Ticket Per Person above 12 years is 100/- only for General Show and with family 0-5 year child is free and 50/- Ticket for 6-12 year child.",
  "rule5": "5. For foreign tourist per person ticket above 12 year is 460 /- and 260/- for 6-12 year child and 0-5 year child free. (All shows and headphone are included.)",
  "rule6": "6. Smoking and Alcohol consumption within the parking and campus is strictly prohibited. Carrying alcohol and banned substances in vehicles is strictly prohibited within the parking and campus.",
  "rule7": "7. Please switch off the mobile phone and cameras in Pratap Gaurav Kendra.",
  "rule8": "8. HUMBLE REQUEST – Your visit to Pratap Gaurav Kendra Rashtriya Tirtha is a pilgrimage to a sacred centre of Bharat’s Cultural traditions and values. We request your support to maintain the peace, dignity and divinity of the complex.",
  "rule9": "9. The management reserves all rights to entry. We apologize for any inconvenience.",
  "mevadSphurtiDirghaTitle": "Mevad Sphurti Dirgha",
  "roboticShowLabel": "Robotic Show",
  "durationTBA": "Duration: TBA",
  "mevadSphurtiDirghaDesc": "This show uses mechanical models to narrate various stories of Mevad. It provides a cinematic experience, showcasing events like the victory of Hammir Chittorgarh.",
  "yeGathaHaiMevadKiTitle": "Ye Gatha Hai Mevad Ki",
  "duration18Mins": "18 Minutes",
  "documentaryShowLabel": "Documentary Show",
  "overviewTitle": "Overview",
  "docShowOverviewDesc": "This documentary show provides a comprehensive overview of the entire history of Mevad in 18 minutes. It offers insights into the sacrifices and continuous dedication to the nation by Mevad.",
  "proudHistoryMewarTitle": "The Proud History of Mewar",
  "proudHistoryMewarDesc": "The history of Mewar is a saga of unmatched courage, sacrifice, and loyalty to the motherland. At Pratap Gaurav Kendra in Udaipur, visitors can explore this incredible journey through immersive exhibits and engaging presentations. Unlike any other museum in Udaipur, this heritage center offers a unique way to experience the pride and valor that shaped India’s cultural and historical identity.",
  "whatMakesPgkSpecialTitle": "What Makes Pratap Gaurav Kendra Special?",
  "whatMakesPgkSpecialDesc": "Unlike a traditional museum in Udaipur that focuses only on artifacts, this center blends technology and storytelling. Here, the history of Mewar is showcased with:",
  "specialBullet1": "Engaging visuals that recreate significant battles and sacrifices.",
  "specialBullet2": "Concise narratives that summarize centuries of history in minutes.",
  "specialBullet3": "Emotional depth that connects visitors with the spirit of the land.",
  "specialBullet4": "National significance highlighting Mewar’s contribution to Indian identity.",
  "whyVisitTitle": "Why Visit?",
  "whyVisitDesc": "If you are planning to explore a museum in Udaipur, here’s why this center should top your list:",
  "whyVisitBullet1": "It presents the history of Mewar in an interactive and inspiring way.",
  "whyVisitBullet2": "Families, students, and tourists gain both knowledge and pride.",
  "whyVisitBullet3": "It is more than a museum—it is a living tribute to courage and culture.",
  "conclusionTitle": "Conclusion",
  "conclusionDesc": "The history of Mewar is a timeless tale of bravery and honor. Pratap Gaurav Kendra ensures that every visitor not only learns about this history but also feels connected to its spirit. For anyone planning to visit a museum in Udaipur, this center offers a unique opportunity to go beyond artifacts and step into the living legacy of Mewar.\n\nVisit Pratap Gaurav Kendra and experience the proud history of Mewar.",
  "faqTitleStandard": "Frequently Asked Questions",
  "faqDocQ1": "What does the history of Mewar include?",
  "faqDocA1": "It covers the origins, architectural achievements, cultural values, and the timeless traditions of bravery and sacrifice that continue to inspire generations.",
  "faqDocQ2": "How is it different from a traditional museum?",
  "faqDocA2": "While regular museums focus on displaying objects, Pratap Gaurav Kendra brings the history of Mewar alive with visuals, sound, and storytelling.",
  "faqDocQ3": "Is this place suitable for children and students?",
  "faqDocA3": "Yes, it simplifies the history of Mewar into engaging formats that young learners can understand easily.",
  "faqDocQ4": "Where is it located?",
  "faqDocA4": "Pratap Gaurav Kendra is situated in Udaipur, Rajasthan, making it a top alternative to a traditional museum in Udaipur.",
  "rajasthanDirghaTitle": "Rajasthan Dirgha",
  "rajasthanDirghaNarrationText": "In this epic, statues of 25 selected warriors, great personalities, saints, and local deities of Rajasthan are showcased...",
  "rajasthanDirghaNarrationLabel": "Rajasthan Dirgha Narration",
  "audioGuideLabel": "Audio Guide",
  "greatPersonalitiesTitle": "The Great Personalities of Rajasthan",
  "greatPersonalitiesDesc1": "In this epic, breathtaking statues of 25 selected warriors, great personalities, saints, and local deities of Rajasthan are proudly showcased. The exhibit serves as a cultural archive, offering a glimpse into the diverse spiritual and martial history of the region.",
  "prominentLocalDeitiesTitle": "Prominent Local Deities",
  "deity1": "Ramdevji",
  "deity2": "Tejaji",
  "deity3": "Gogaji",
  "heroicFiguresTitle": "Heroic Figures & Warriors",
  "warrior1": "Durgadas Rathore",
  "warrior2": "Hamir Chauhan",
  "warrior3": "Rao Chandrasen",
  "warrior4": "Rao Shekha Ji",
  "moreLegendaryFigures": "And many more legendary figures.",
  "greatPersonalitiesDesc2": "More than just a visual display, this epic dirgha provides thoroughly documented records of the life stories, teachings, and monumental sacrifices of these local deities, saints, and warriors.",
  "pratapHeroTitle": "Maharana Pratap: The Lion of\nMewar",
  "narrationBattleOfHaldighati": "Narration: The Battle of Haldighati",
  "keyEventsTitle": "Key Events",
  "haldighatiRecreation": "Haldighati Battle\nRecreation",
  "chetaksSacrifice": "Chetak's Sacrifice",
  "pratapsCoronation": "Pratap's Coronation",
  "mewadRatanDirghaTitle": "Mewad Ratan Dirgha",
  "mewadRatanNarrationText": "The major warriors and heroic women of Mewar are displayed in this epic. Starting with Bappa Rawal, it extends to the warriors, saints, and heroic women...",
  "mewadRatanNarrationLabel": "Mewad Ratan Dirgha Narration",
  "prideOfMewarTitle": "The Pride of Mewar",
  "prideOfMewarDesc1": "The major warriors and heroic women of Mewar are displayed in this epic exhibit. Starting with Bappa Rawal, it extends to the warriors, saints, and heroic women during the reign of Maharana Raj Singh. The epic showcases the military valor and spiritual inclinations of Mewar’s army.",
  "prideOfMewarDesc2": "It provides concise information about the history and culture of the Guhilots’ kingdom in Mewar from its inception to the 18th century.",
  "significantFiguresTitle": "Significant Figures Displayed",
  "significantFiguresDesc": "The dirgha includes majestic statues and depictions of the following historical icons:",
  "mewadFigure1": "Bappa Rawal & Harit Rashi",
  "mewadFigure2": "Padmavati, Gaura & Badal",
  "mewadFigure3": "Satyavrat Chunda",
  "mewadFigure4": "Maharana Kumbhakarna (Rana Kumbha)",
  "mewadFigure5": "Maharana Sangram Singh I (Rana Sanga)",
  "mewadFigure6": "Panna Dhay",
  "mewadFigure7": "Jaymal Medtia & Patta Sisodia",
  "mewadFigure8": "Kalla Rathore",
  "mewadFigure9": "Meera Bai",
  "mewadFigure10": "Maharana Uday Singh II",
  "mewadFigure11": "Bhamashah & Rana Punja",
  "mewadFigure12": "Hakeem Khan Sur",
  "mewadFigure13": "Maharana Amar Singh & Maharana Raj Singh",
  "mewadFigure14": "Hadi Rani",
  "krantikariDirghaTitle": "Krantikari Dirgha",
  "krantikariNarrationText": "This epic, located in the center of the Pratap Gaurav Kendra, showcases the stories of brave warriors from the Indian independence struggle...",
  "krantikariNarrationLabel": "Krantikari Dirgha Narration",
  "heroesOfIndependenceTitle": "Heroes of the Independence Struggle",
  "heroesOfIndependenceDesc1": "Located in the center of the Pratap Gaurav Kendra, this epic exhibit showcases the stories of brave warriors from the Indian independence struggle using magnificent statues.",
  "heroesOfIndependenceDesc2": "The epic covers the crucial period from 1857 to 1947, presenting the timeless tales of valor and sacrifice through stunning sculptural representations.",
  "keyHighlightsTitle": "Key Highlights",
  "krantikariHighlight1": "Central Location: Situated prominently at the heart of the Kendra.",
  "krantikariHighlight2": "Historical Timeline: Covers the monumental era from the First War of Independence (1857) to India's Freedom (1947).",
  "krantikariHighlight3": "Sculptural Storytelling: Tales of valor brought to life through incredibly detailed, lifelike statues.",
  "krantikariHighlight4": "Tribute to Martyrs: Dedicated entirely to the brave revolutionaries who fought against colonial rule.",
  "haldighatiDirghaTitle": "Haldighati Vijay Yudh Dirgha",
  "haldighatiNarrationText1": "The Haldighati Vijay Yuddh Dirgha presents a powerful visual narration of the historic Battle of Haldighati...",
  "haldighatiNarrationLabel": "Battle of Haldighati Narration",
  "exploreLegacyTitle": "Explore the Legacy of Maharana Pratap",
  "exploreLegacyDesc1": "Pratap Gaurav Kendra Udaipur offers a unique journey into the heroic life and achievements of Maharana Pratap, a symbol of courage and resilience in Indian history. This site is highly relevant for history lovers, tourists, and students keen on exploring the rich heritage of Rajasthan. As a prominent museum in Udaipur, the Maharana Pratap Museum Udaipur provides immersive exhibits that highlight the king’s struggles and victories, making it an essential destination for cultural exploration.",
  "highlightsMuseumTitle": "Highlights of the Museum",
  "highlightMuseum1": "The Maharana Pratap Museum displays a curated collection of historic artifacts, paintings, and weaponry.",
  "highlightMuseum2": "Themed galleries recreate significant moments from Maharana Pratap’s battles and court life.",
  "highlightMuseum3": "Rare manuscripts and photographs offer insights into 16th-century Rajput culture.",
  "highlightMuseum4": "Interactive touchscreens provide engaging narratives and detailed information.",
  "highlightMuseum5": "Planning a city tour? Don’t miss these essential Udaipur City Tour Places.",
  "visitorTipsTitle": "Visitor Tips and Experience",
  "visitorTip1": "Visit early in the morning or late afternoon to enjoy a quieter, more personalized experience.",
  "visitorTip2": "Photography enthusiasts will find many scenic and historically rich spots for capturing unique shots.",
  "visitorTip3": "Local guides and tour operators offer special heritage tours including Pratap Gaurav Kendra and nearby attractions.",
  "exploreLegacyDesc2": "The Haldighati Vijay Yuddh Dirgha presents a powerful visual narration of the historic Battle of Haldighati fought between Maharana Pratap of Mewar and the Mughal forces. This gallery beautifully showcases the courage, military strategy, and unbreakable determination of the Rajput warriors who defended their homeland against a powerful empire. Through lifelike installations and artistic storytelling, the Dirgha preserves a proud chapter of Indian history and brings the spirit of honor and resistance to life.",
  "faqHaldighatiQ1": "What time does Pratap Gaurav Kendra open and close?",
  "faqHaldighatiA1": "Visitors can explore the museum from 10:00 AM to 5:30 PM every day except on select holidays.",
  "faqHaldighatiQ2": "Is the Museum accessible for visitors with disabilities?",
  "faqHaldighatiA2": "Yes, the museum is designed to be inclusive with features like ramps and assistance services.",
  "faqHaldighatiQ3": "Are guided tours available at the museum?",
  "faqHaldighatiA3": "Yes, guided tours are offered in various languages and can be booked in advance.",
  "faqHaldighatiQ4": "Can school groups participate in educational programs?",
  "faqHaldighatiA4": "Definitely, the museum regularly organizes tailored educational visits for students of all ages.",
  "faqHaldighatiQ5": "Is photography permitted inside?",
  "faqHaldighatiA5": "Photography is allowed in designated areas, but flash and video recording may be restricted as per museum rules.",
  "charitraPradarshaneeTitle": "Maharana Pratap Charitra Pradarshanee",
  "charitraNarrationText1": "The life story of Maharana Pratap from birth to death is displayed through paintings in five rooms. Whether it is the birthplace of Pratap...",
  "charitraNarrationLabel": "Charitra Pradarshanee Narration",
  "journeyThroughLegendTitle": "A Journey Through a Legend’s Life",
  "charitraDesc1": "The life story of Maharana Pratap from birth to death is displayed through paintings in five rooms. Whether it is the birthplace of Pratap in Kumbhalgarh or scenes depicting Pratap freeing Abdul Rahim Khan-Khana’s family or the sacrifice of his loyal horse Chetak, these scenes provide a vivid portrayal through paintings, offering viewers an immersive experience.",
  "charitraDesc2": "A striking highlight is the Maharana Pratap statue that stands tall, symbolizing his unwavering spirit and bravery. The Charitra Pradarshanee offers a visually captivating and educational experience that brings the legendary Rajput warrior’s life to light.",
  "grandStatueTitle": "The Grand Maharana Pratap Statue",
  "grandStatueDesc": "Standing tall inside the Pradarshanee, this magnificent statue depicts Maharana Pratap mounted on his loyal horse, Chetak. It is a true tribute to the indomitable Rajput spirit.",
  "statueBullet1": "Represents courage, sacrifice, and honor.",
  "statueBullet2": "Serves as an inspiration for future generations.",
  "statueBullet3": "A landmark that draws visitors from across India.",
  "charitraHighlight1": "Battle Dioramas: Life-like displays narrating the Battle of Haldighati and other decisive moments.",
  "charitraHighlight2": "Weapons and Artifacts: Replicas of the swords, shields, and armors used by Rajput warriors.",
  "charitraHighlight3": "Cultural Galleries: Exhibits showcasing Rajputana lifestyle, costumes, and traditions.",
  "charitraHighlight4": "Freedom Fighters Section: Honoring India’s heroes who followed Maharana Pratap’s path of courage.",
  "whyVisitUdaipurTitle": "Why Visit During Your Udaipur Trip?",
  "visitBullet1": "Establish a deeper connection with Rajasthan’s history.",
  "visitBullet2": "A chance to learn about Maharana Pratap’s unmatched spirit of freedom.",
  "visitBullet3": "An inspiring cultural experience unlike any other tourist site.",
  "charitraConclusion": "More than a museum, the Maharana Pratap Charitra Pradarshanee is a place of inspiration. The exhibits and the statue ignite a sense of patriotism and pride in every visitor. It is a reminder that true leadership lies in selflessness, resilience, and honor.",
  "faqCharitraQ1": "What is the Charitra Pradarshanee famous for?",
  "faqCharitraA1": "It is famous for its magnificent Maharana Pratap statue and detailed galleries that bring to life the legacy of Maharana Pratap and the history of Mewar.",
  "faqCharitraQ2": "Where is the Maharana Pratap Statue located?",
  "faqCharitraA2": "The grand Maharana Pratap statue is located at the Charitra Pradarshanee inside Pratap Gaurav Kendra, Udaipur.",
  "faqCharitraQ3": "How long does it take to explore?",
  "faqCharitraA3": "Visitors usually spend 2–3 hours exploring the museum, statue, and exhibits in detail.",
  "faqCharitraQ4": "Is it suitable for families and children?",
  "faqCharitraA4": "Yes, the museum is family-friendly and offers a wonderful educational experience for children and adults alike.",
  "faqCharitraQ5": "Why is the Maharana Pratap Statue important?",
  "faqCharitraA5": "It is a cultural landmark that symbolizes bravery and sacrifice, keeping alive the story of Maharana Pratap for generations.",
  "bharatMataMandirTitle": "Bharat Mata Mandir",
  "bharatMataNarrationText": "In India, the tradition of worshiping Gram Devi, Sthan Dev, and Matru Devi has been ancient. In Mewar, Jagadamba is worshiped as Rashtra Shyamala, and a temple dedicated to her is located on the way to Kailashpuri...",
  "bharatMataNarrationLabel": "Bharat Mata Mandir Narration",
  "worshipingRashtraDeviTitle": "Worshiping the Rashtra Devi",
  "bharatMataDesc1": "In India, the tradition of worshiping Gram Devi, Sthan Dev, and Matru Devi (Mother Goddess) has been ancient. In Mewar, Jagadamba is worshiped as Rashtra Shyamala, and a temple dedicated to her is located on the way to Kailashpuri near Udaipur. In local tradition, she is referred to as Rathasena Mata.",
  "bharatMataDesc2": "This is possibly the oldest temple dedicated to the Rashtra Devi (Mother of India) in the country. During the struggle for independence, Bankim Chandra Chattopadhyay, in his novel \"Anandamath,\" first called for the worship of Bharat Mata and presented an image of the Rashtra Devi, with the anthem \"Vande Mataram\" taking the form of the national song.",
  "appearanceArchitectureTitle": "Appearance & Architecture",
  "bharatMataBullet1": "Adorned in an orange-colored sari, holding a saffron flag in her hand.",
  "bharatMataBullet2": "Installed majestically on her vehicle, a lion.",
  "bharatMataBullet3": "The temple’s sanctum sanctorum is uniquely octagonal and situated at an elevation.",
  "bharatMataBullet4": "Visitors must climb 71 stairs to reach the temple, symbolizing the ascent to national glory and instilling a deep sense of pride.",
  "meditationRoomTitle": "Meditation Room",
  "meditationRoomDesc": "Just below the temple, a serene meditation room has been set up. After exploring the Pratap Gaurav Kendra, visitors can meditate and contemplate in this beautiful blue-white space, experiencing otherworldly and spiritual bliss.",
